RTGZ3 - the Zorro III RTG board's driver (MiSTer.card 0.3)

One driver for the A4000 Minimig cores: MiST/SiDi/NeptUNO (MinimigAGA)
and MiSTer (AMIGA4000-MiSTer, Maximig). It finds the board through
autoconfig (mfr $139C, product $30, 16 MB) and tells the two video
backends apart by the board's ID register.

On the SiDi: Fast RAM at the most in the OSD (the board replaces the
Zorro II RAM). xSysInfo's Boards must show $139C/$30, 16M.

From a Shell:
  Execute RTGZ3:Install     installs it (keeps the old files as .old)
  Execute RTGZ3:Restore     puts the old files back

Then reboot and make the screen modes in Prefs/Picasso96Mode
(8 and 16 bits on MiST/SiDi; also 24/32 bits on MiSTer).

Icons: Install, Restore and Test run with C:IconX (double-click).
Test shows what RTGTest sees (the board, its ID, the driver's counters).

Drawer Picasso96: tools from Aminet's driver/video/Picasso96.lha 2.0
(Picasso96Mode, FliP96, AttachSettings, Debug/CheckBoards, P96Speed),
shareware by Tobias Abt and Alexander Kneer, and MiSTer: the Picasso96
monitor with BOARDTYPE=MiSTer, to drag to DEVS:Monitors if you have none.
